          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The concept of
            %em analytic spectrum
            is a realization of the concept of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum+%28geometry%29"} spectrum (geometry)
            in the context of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-archimedean+analytic+geometry"} non-archimedean analytic geometry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affinoid+algebra"} affinoid algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            over a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-archimedean+field"} non-archimedean field
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum+of+a+commutative+ring"} spectrum of a commutative ring
            whose points are
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prime+ideals"} prime ideals
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/maximal+ideals"} maximal ideals
            does not produce a sensible space that admits
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/analytic+geometry"} analytic geometry
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to \mathbb{R}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/seminorms"} seminorms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mo ≥
                      %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\vert -\vert} \colon A \to \mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}
            bounded by the norm on the given field.
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Spec
                    %mi an
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec_{an}(A)
            is the set of all such multiplicative seminorms, then for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %msub
                    %mi Spec
                    %mi an
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in Spec_{an}(A)
            a point one writes the corresponding seminorm as
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mo −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\vert - \vert}_x
            and thinks of it as being the norm on the function algebra on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec(A)
            which is given by “evaluating functions at
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            and then applying the field norm to that”.
          %p
            One turns this
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Spec
                    %mi an
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec_{an}(A)
            into a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            in the usual way by choosing the weakest topology such that under this assignment the original elements of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            become
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous function
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Spec
                      %mi an
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec_{an}(A)
          %p
            Globalizing this analytic spectrum construction leads to the concept of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Berkovich+analytic+space"} Berkovich analytic space
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normed+ring"} normed ring
            %em analytic spectrum
            or
            %em Berkovich spectrum
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Spec
                    %mi an
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec_an A
            is the set of all non-zero multiplicative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/seminorms"} seminorms
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            when equipped with the weakest topology such that all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functions"} functions
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Spec
                    %mi an
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo +
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Spec_{an} A \to \mathbb{R}_+
          %p of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ↦
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  x \mapsto {\vert x(a)\vert}
          %p
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in A
            are
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is equipped with the structure of a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Banach+ring"} Banach ring
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bounded+map"} bounded
            multiplicative seminorms.
          %p
            So a point in the analytic spectrum of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            corresponds to a non-zero
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  {\Vert -\Vert} : A \to \mathbb{R}
          %p
            to the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x, y \in A
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mo ≥
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\Vert x \Vert} \geq 0
                ;
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mi x
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mo =
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\Vert x y \Vert} = {\Vert x \Vert} {\Vert y \Vert}
                ;
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mi x
                        %mo +
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mo ≤
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mo +
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\Vert x + y \Vert} \leq {\Vert x \Vert} + {\Vert y \Vert}
          %p
            and boundedness means that there exists
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo &gt;
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \gt 0
            such that for all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in A
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                  %mo ≤
                  %mi C
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi A
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  {\Vert x\Vert} \leq C {\vert x \vert}_A
                  \\,.
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Berkovich09"} Berkovich 09, def. 1.2.3
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#affine_line Affine line
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k[T]
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polynomial+ring"} polynomial ring
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            in one generator,
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔸
                    %mi k
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi Spec
                    %mi an
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbb{A}_k := Spec_{an} k[T]
          %p
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/analytic+affine+line"} analytic affine line
            over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
          %p
            If
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo =
                    %mi ℂ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k = \mathbb{C}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔸
                    %mi k
                  %mo =
                  %mi ℂ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{A}_k = \mathbb{C}
            is the ordinary
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+plane"} complex plane
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum+%28geometry%29"} spectrum (geometry)
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/analytic+geometry"}> analytic geometry
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/analytic+space"} analytic space
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/p-adic+geometry"} p-adic geometry
          %h2#references References
          %h3#original Original
          %p The notion originates in
          %ul
            %li#Berkovich90
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vladimir+Berkovich"}> Vladimir Berkovich
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Spectral theory and analytic geometry over non-Archimedean fields
          %h3#expositions_and_lecture_notes Expositions and Lecture notes
          %p Introductory exposition of the Berkovich analytic spectrum includes
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sarah+Brodsky"}> Sarah Brodsky
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Non-archimedean geometry
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://math.berkeley.edu/~sstich/MAT_274/Math_274_3_Feb_2012.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Scott+Carnahan"}> Scott Carnahan
                ,
                %em Berkovich spaces I
                (
                %a{:href => "http://sbseminar.wordpress.com/2007/09/18/berkovich-spaces-i/"}> web
                )
            %li#Poineau07
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J%C3%A9r%C3%B4me+Poineau"}> Jérôme Poineau
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Global analytic geometry
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.ems-ph.org/journals/newsletter/pdf/2007-09-65.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fr%C3%A9d%C3%A9ric+Paugam"}> Frédéric Paugam
                , section 2.1.4 of
                %em Global analytic geometry and the functional equation
                (2010) (
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.jussieu.fr/~fpaugam/documents/enseignement/master-global-analytic-geometry.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li#Berkovich09
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vladimir+Berkovich"}> Vladimir Berkovich
                , section 1 of
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Non-archimedean analytic spaces
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Advanced School on
                    = succeed "-adic" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi p
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.wisdom.weizmann.ac.il/~vova/Trieste_2009.pdf"} pdf
